{"duration_api_ms": 64769, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "a485e2a4-9f32-4c0a-be93-fd222b514390", "total_cost_usd": 0.01940956, "usage": {"input_tokens": 50, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 33038, "cache_read_input_tokens": 892731, "output_tokens": 12695, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2952}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 33038}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 680, "cache_read_input_tokens": 48285, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 572, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 572, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-5-5": {"inputTokens": 50, "outputTokens": 12695, "cacheReadInputTokens": 892731, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 33038, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.01940956, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 2952, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 35, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`on_setattr` hooks can now be generator functions. The spec's check passes: `.venv/bin/python -m pytest -q tests/test_compat.py tests/test_setattr.py` gives 52 passed, 1 xfailed. The full suite gives 1399 passed, 7 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\nChanges:\n- **`src/attr/_compat.py`**: added `_IS_GENERATOR_RESULTS` and `_lazy_is_generator`. The result is cached per hook, and unhashable hooks fall back to an uncached check.\n- **`src/attr/_make.py`**: `add_setattr` stores `(attr, hook, is_generator)` per hook. The generated `__setattr__` runs the generator's pre-yield code, sets the yielded value, then resumes it. A second yield closes the generator and raises `RuntimeError`. The `attrib` docstring has the 26.2.0 note.\n- **`src/attr/_next_gen.py`**: the `define` and `field` docstrings describe generator hooks and carry the 26.2.0 note.\n- **`src/attr/setters.py`**: a warning in `pipe`'s docstring says generator functions are not allowed there.\n- **`src/attrs/__init__.pyi`**: `_OnSetAttrType` also accepts a callable returning `Generator[Any]`.\n- **`docs/examples.md`**: new \"Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes\" section with the doctest from the spec.\n\nDecisions and deviations:\n- The spec names `_ClassBuilder._make_own_setattr`, but this tree has no such method. The logic lives in `add_setattr`, so I changed that method.\n- The `_OnSetAttrType` change is a union of the plain and generator callable types, which is how I read \"also accepts.\"\n\nLint: `ruff format --check` is clean. `ruff check` reports one error, RUF063 at `_compat.py:60` (`cls.__dict__` access in `_get_annotations`). That line predates my change, so I left it.", "ttft_ms": 1602, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 83224, "uuid": "e609c8a9-630c-42bb-8913-bb4c45eb9b1d", "ttft_stream_ms": 1274, "time_to_request_ms": 492, "first_content_frame_ms": 1274, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
